  "summary": "Rogue, modified ScreenConnect clients spawn wscript.exe to execute a four-stage VBScript chain (1.vbs-4.vbs) that profiles the host, downloads AES-encrypted payload bundles from Dropbox, and persists via a WindowsServiceHost Run key pointing to WindowsServiceHost.vbs. The backdoored client registers the same VBS stagers into a ScreenConnect file-transfer message with its action set to Run, propagating the chain worm-like to every newly connected Host session. Huntress ties the activity to C2 infrastructure 45.13.237[.]190 / tele-sync.opik[.]net and secondary RMM tools such as UltraViewer.",
